## Tier 1: before the deadline (29 Aug AoE)

### 1.1 The measured-alignment panel  [~2 days, the single biggest move]

The paper's central object, the alignment matrix R and its lambda_max, is
currently hypothetical everywhere. Make it measured once, on real models:

- Data: public per-item eval outputs. First choice: the released data from
  Kim, Garg, Peng & Garg (ICML 2025), built for exactly this. Fallbacks:
  HELM per-instance JSONs; OpenLLM leaderboard per-sample dumps.
- Method: per model, form the error-indicator vector over common items;
  compute pairwise error correlation r_ij; report lambda_max(R_hat) as a
  measured effective learner count against the model count N; split
  within-provider vs cross-provider; fit s_hat from the block structure.
- Deliverable: one heatmap figure (R_hat ordered by provider, lambda_max
  and N in the title), one MEASURED row in the panel table, one honest
  caveat sentence (error correlation is an output-side proxy for
  feedback-direction alignment, which is the object (H3) says firms
  retrain against).
- Expected story: same-provider blocks with high r, moderate cross-provider
  r, i.e. the "plurality vendor" topology the clustered example warns
  about, found in the wild. If lambda_max(R_hat) comes out well below N
  but well above 1, that number is the talk's headline.

Why this is the difference-maker: it converts the paper from "a theory
with a simulator anchor" to "a theory whose key quantity was measured on
350 real models," it is what the v1 review asked for, and no competing
submission in this niche will have it.

### 1.2 The nonlinearity ablation  [~1 day]

The stated largest gap is linearization (A1). Turn the adjective into a
measurement: add a saturating response (tanh with scale lambda) to the
reference environment, sweep lambda from 0, plot the measured stability
boundary against the Theorem 2 prediction. One small figure or four inline
numbers. A graceful, monotone departure is the claim "the closed forms
govern a neighbourhood" made quantitative, and it preempts the one
criticism every theory reviewer will type.

