## Tier 2: camera-ready and the workshop itself (Sep to Dec)

### 2.1 The artifact release
De-anonymize: uncomment the repository URL, drop `hypersetup{draft=true}`,
add the `final` option. Ship the repo with a one-command
`make reproduce` that runs all 525 certificate assertions and regenerates
every figure from the committed result JSONs, and a CI badge that runs the
certificates on every push. Reviewers talk about papers whose numbers they
can regenerate in five minutes; workshop organizers remember them.

### 2.2 The talk (orals are won here)
- One-figure story: open on the substitution frontier (rho_c, s), the
  paper's most policy-legible object.
- Three-number elevator pitch: "fifty firms, one vendor, dynamically
  ~1 + 49*kappa learners"; "past crowding 9, no cadence is safe";
  "coverage (1 - 1/m_N)/e, the imperfect-vaccine law."
- Say the provenance-channel asymmetry out loud: your competitor's choice
  of vendor consumes your step budget without them entering.
- Prepare the two hard questions in advance with slides in the deck's
  appendix: (H1) rank-one deviation, and "why should I believe a dry run."

### 2.3 The demo (optional, memorable)
A small interactive page: sliders for N, kappa, s, theta; live m_N,
K_max, rho_c*; the phase diagram recolors. The entire theory module is
closed-form, so this is an afternoon with the existing formulas, and it is
the kind of thing that makes a poster the one people stand around.

### 2.4 Extend the measured panel
If 1.1 lands, extend it for camera-ready: N_eff by provider over time
(leaderboard snapshots exist), which turns "concentration is rising" from
a talking point into a time series.

